/-!
# The higher-multiplicity marked-kernel reduction

Small displacement bounds multiplicity by two. The proved same-vector
alternative thus gives the exact fixed line at higher multiplicity. The
quotient-transvection endgame is checked conditionally; construction of the
stabilized orthogonal constituents and their model recognition remains open.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith G.10.16 and G.11.8--9, printed pp.363--369.
-/
